# Translations (reuse and low churn)

Details: `doc/i18n.rst`. Catalogs: `po/xcsoar.pot` and `po/*.po`.

## Reuse strings

Do not add a new `_()` / `N_()` / `C_()` string if the same English already
exists. Search `po/xcsoar.pot` and existing call sites first.

Near-duplicates (`OK` vs `Ok`, extra punctuation, slightly different
phrasing) create 33 extra translations. Match the existing msgid.

Use `C_()` / `NC_()` only when the same English needs a different
translation by role. Prefer existing contexts (`Button`, `Menu`,
`Setting`, `Status`, `InfoBox`, …).

Do not mark log messages for translation.

## Low-churn catalog updates

After source changes, run `make update-po` (`tools/update_po_low_churn.py`).

The `.po` / `.pot` diff must **only add new msgid/msgstr entries** (and
fill those new empty `msgstr` values). Do not:

- rewrap or reorder untouched entries
- rewrite existing `msgstr`
- bulk-save with `polib` or any full-file rewrap
- add `#:` location comments

Fill new empty `msgstr` across languages when possible. Leave existing
translations alone unless they are wrong.
